{"t": 1794115222.2579823, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline 8812 (main, a91c2e0) is red because the `test:contract` job (77104) fails on `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`:\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nRoot cause: `billing/invoice.py` formatted the sequence as a plain integer (`f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`), so no zero-padding was applied. The ERP v2 contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to six digits.\n\nFix: format the sequence with `{seq:06d}`:\n\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    # ERP v2 / FIN-77: the sequence part is zero-padded to six digits.\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerified locally: `invoice_number(2026, 42)` now returns `INV-2026-000042`, and other values (e.g. `7 -> INV-2026-000007`, `123456 -> INV-2026-123456`) format correctly. The `lint` job already passes; with this change the contract job should pass and pipeline 8812 should go green.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
